      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 768,
        "content": "## Mail to Lexware via API\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow monitors an email inbox for new messages, extracts their attachments, and uploads those files to Lexware using the Lexware files API. After the upload step, it sends a Pushover notification so the user knows the process completed.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the IMAP email credentials and mailbox/folder settings on the Email Trigger node.\n- Review the Split Attachments code to ensure it matches the email attachment structure and file types you expect.\n- Configure the HTTP Request node with Lexware API authentication and verify the POST endpoint https://api.lexware.io/v1/files is correct.\n- Set up Pushover credentials, target user/device settings, and the notification message content.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can customize attachment filtering in the code node, adjust the Lexware upload endpoint or request fields, and change the Pushover message to include details such as file name, sender, or upload status."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ea0357c1-e995-409b-9521-3e51aaa9df50",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -592,
        -176
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 416,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Read and split mail\n\nReceives incoming email through IMAP and uses custom code to split out attachments so each file can be processed for upload."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "10c5a20d-5e1c-495e-ae2c-9e36a5968c98",
